<article class="env-lemma" id="05YS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05YS">Lemma <span data-tag="05YS">97.14.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Then $\mathcal{H}_ d(X)$ is an algebraic stack. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The $1$-morphism 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{H}_ d(X) \longrightarrow \mathcal{H}_ d  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is representable by algebraic spaces according to Lemma <a href="/tag/05YJ" data-tag="05YJ">97.12.6</a>. The stack $\mathcal{H}_ d$ is an algebraic stack according to Proposition <a href="/tag/05YQ" data-tag="05YQ">97.13.2</a>. Hence $\mathcal{H}_ d(X)$ is an algebraic stack by Algebraic Stacks, Lemma <a href="/tag/05UM" data-tag="05UM">94.15.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>